2. Data Governance & Storage Architecture

(Focus: Unity Catalog, Data Separation, Metadata Governance)

Unity Catalog Strategy

* Dedicated catalogs per tenant/team
* Standardized schema hierarchy
* Ownership boundaries clearly defined

Example:

* catalog = tenant/team
* schema = domain/application
* tables = datasets

Storage Isolation

* Separate ADLS Gen2 containers/storage accounts per tenant
* External locations mapped through Unity Catalog
* Managed vs external table strategy

Data Access Controls

* Table-level and column-level permissions
* Row-level security requirements
* PII/classification handling strategy

Metadata & Lineage Governance

* Enable lineage tracking
* Data classification tags
* Naming conventions for datasets and schemas

Open Questions

* Will storage separation be container-level or account-level?
* Will tenants be allowed to create schemas dynamically?
* Who owns catalog lifecycle management?

⸻

3. Compute Governance & Cost Management

(Focus: Cluster Policies, Serverless, Chargeback)

Cluster Policy Enforcement

* Enforced cluster policies for:
    * node types
    * auto-scaling
    * runtime versions
    * idle termination
    * tagging standards
* Restrict unrestricted compute creation

Serverless Compute Governance

* Define approved workloads for serverless usage
* Evaluate tenant isolation guarantees in shared serverless environments
* Clarify supported access modes

Cost Allocation & Chargeback

* Mandatory tags:
    * team_name
    * cost_center
    * environment
    * application
* Usage reporting via:
    * system.billing
    * system.compute
    * Azure cost management

Environment Strategy

* Dev/Test/Prod separation model
* Clarify:
    * Single workspace with logical isolation
    * Multiple workspaces per environment
    * Catalog-level separation

Open Questions

* Can serverless usage be attributed cleanly per tenant?
* Is serverless approved for production workloads?
* What workloads require dedicated clusters?

